-## Phase 1 — runner builds and boots on macOS arm64
+## Phase 1 — runner builds and boots on macOS arm64 (DONE 2026-10-09, FreeBIOS)
 
-Goal: the existing, proven firmware path runs on this Mac. No Rhythm Heaven yet.
+Result: `nds_runner` builds on macOS arm64 (Apple clang 21, Ninja) and boots
+Rhythm Heaven to its title screen ("Touch me!" on the bottom screen) on the
+dump-free FreeBIOS path, headless, in ~2.5 s for 200M ARM9 cycles. Both
+framebuffers are non-empty at 600 VBlanks and the pixel counts reproduce
+exactly across runs. The suite's `--runner` stage encodes this.
 
-1. Make the runner configure on macOS: drop mingw-only link flags, remove the
-   `F:/Projects/recomp-ui` default, make `host_unwind_x64`/`host_profile`
-   compile out (or use a Mach-O unwinder) off Windows, build with
-   `-DNDS_SDL_BACKEND=SDL3`, `NDS_3D_RENDERER=soft`.
-2. Gate Tier-2 / live-overlay (`live_overlay*.cpp`) behind a CMake option,
-   default OFF on Apple targets. This is also the iOS prerequisite.
-3. Produce banks for the BIOSes (retail per D1, else FreeBIOS) and boot to the
-   firmware menu with mouse touch.
-4. Build the oracle (`oracle/setup-melonds.sh` → `ndsref`) on macOS and run G1.
-   Use `melonDS.app` (1.1) only for eyeballing, never as the diff reference.
+Framework changes that made it build:
 
-Exit: G1 passes on macOS with `tier3_insns9 = tier3_insns7 = 0`; menu is
-interactive with the mouse.
+- `NDS_RETAIL_BIOS_BANKS=OFF` links without `arm9_bios.c`/`arm7_bios.c`
+  (empty retail dispatch tables; the retail path fails at hash verification).
+- `live_overlay_platform.cpp`: the non-Windows/non-Linux branch referenced
+  undeclared locals; guarded so Apple builds compile (live overlay stays off).
+- The runner needs a `recomp-ui` checkout (`RECOMP_UI_ROOT` / `-DNDS_RECOMP_UI_ROOT`);
+  the default pointed at `F:/Projects/recomp-ui`.
+
+Recipe (see `tools/rh_suite.py --runner` for the automated form):
+
+```
+nds_recompile --config bios/freebios9.toml --bin third_party/freebios/drastic_bios_arm9.bin --out G --bank freebios_arm9
+nds_recompile --config bios/freebios7.toml --bin third_party/freebios/drastic_bios_arm7.bin --out G --bank freebios_arm7
+cmake -G Ninja -S runner -B B -DNDS_SDL_BACKEND=NONE -DNDS_BOOTSTRAP_FIRMWARE=ON \
+  -DNDS_RETAIL_BIOS_BANKS=OFF -DNDS_ENABLE_COMPUTE_RENDERER=OFF \
+  -DNDS_GENERATED_DIR=G -DNDS_RECOMP_UI_ROOT=<recomp-ui>
+nds_runner . 200000000 --freebios --generated-firmware --boot direct --rom <rom> --no-save
+```
+
+Corrections to the earlier plan:
+
+- **FreeBIOS has no firmware menu.** `--freebios` requires `--boot direct` and a
+  ROM. G1 (firmware traversal vs `ndsref`) and "boot the real menu" therefore
+  need the retail dumps; they are not available on this path.
+- The Phase 2 title screen was reached **with no title banks**: everything ran
+  through the Tier-3 dirty-RAM interpreter (the permitted correctness floor).
+  So "boots" is real but it is not yet *recompiled* execution.
+- `--boot direct` skips the real BIOS/firmware card boot. It is the project's
+  documented opt-in no-dump path; it is not the LLE boot the principles require
+  for accuracy claims.
+- The save type still defaults to 8 KiB EEPROM (`[save] cartridge backup: eeprom,
+  8192`); unknown, not verified.
+
+Still to do for this phase (needs retail dumps or an SDL3 install): SDL3
+windowed/interactive build, touch via mouse, `ndsref` build and G1.
 
 ## Phase 2 — cartridge boot of Rhythm Heaven (LLE)
 
+> Direct-boot title screen already reached in Phase 1 (via Tier 3). What remains
+> here is the *real* card boot (needs retail BIOS/firmware) and the save type.
+
 1. Boot the ROM through the real BIOS/firmware/card path (`startup_mode =
    automatic`; secure area re-encrypt already exists). Watch
    `dispatch_misses.log` and the cart ring to the first game frame.
